## Source of truth

- Follow the **closest** `AGENTS.md` to the paths you edit: repo root → [AGENTS.md](../../../AGENTS.md); under `client/` → [client/AGENTS.md](../../../client/AGENTS.md); under `server/` → [server/AGENTS.md](../../../server/AGENTS.md); design-system code → [core/design-system AGENTS.md](../../../client/core/design-system/src/commonMain/kotlin/dev/kigya/headway/core/designSystem/AGENTS.md).
- Do not paraphrase large sections of those files here—obey them.
- For **project context** (current focus, stack summary, patterns overview), read [.ai/cursor/memory-bank/](../memory-bank/) when starting non-trivial work. It does not override `AGENTS.md` or these rules.
- When **Serena MCP** is available, prefer Serena’s symbolic navigation and targeted edits before broad repository-wide reads; use **Repomix** only for deliberate compact snapshots ([.ai/docs/ai-workflow.md](../../docs/ai-workflow.md)).

## Visibility

- Default `internal`; widen visibility only when another module truly needs the symbol.

## Hygiene

- No `TODO` / `FIXME` / `STOPSHIP`, no `TODO()` / `NotImplementedError`, no `println` / `print` in production code.
- No `!!` without a proven, tightly scoped invariant and no safe alternative.
- No `lateinit` unless there is no cleaner option and the user explicitly requires it.

## Imports

- No wildcard imports except `java.util.*` when absolutely necessary.

## Style (Kotlin)

- Trailing commas on every multiline declaration and call site.
- Named arguments when a call has 4+ arguments.
- `asSequence()` for 3+ chained collection operations.
- Expression bodies for single-return functions.
- Line length under 120; cyclomatic complexity at or below 13; functions at most 6 parameters; constructors at most 7.

## `when`

- No `else` branch for exhaustive sealed types, enums, or boolean subjects.

## Null-safety

- Prefer `as?` + `?:` over unsafe casts.
- Snapshot mutable nullable properties into a local `val` before null-checking.
- Do not use `?.` on non-null types.
- Compare strings with `==` / `!=`, not `===` / `!==`.
- Use `map.getValue("key")` or `map.getOrDefault(...)`—never `map["key"]!!`.

## Exceptions (Kotlin, general)

- Throw specific types with message or cause—never generic `Exception`.
- Do not `catch` and immediately rethrow unchanged.
- Do not throw in `toString`, `hashCode`, `equals`, or `finalize`.
- Use multiple `catch` blocks—do not `is`-check inside a single `catch`.
- Exception types must be `class`, not `object`.

## Coroutines

- Do not mark a function `suspend` unless it actually suspends.
- Functions returning `Flow` must not be `suspend`.
- Do not mix `suspend` with `CoroutineScope` receiver.
- Use `delay()` instead of `Thread.sleep` in coroutine code.

## Comments

- No code comments; KDoc allowed for public APIs only.

## Dependencies

- Do not add new heavy dependencies without explicit user approval.

## Lessons loop (critical)

- After fixing a **user-reported** mistake: if the fix is **reusable** (would help future edits, not a one-off typo), append one concise entry to [lessons-learned.mdc](lessons-learned.mdc) using that file’s format (Rule / Why / Bad / Correct).
- Do not duplicate an existing lesson; merge or extend if the root cause is the same.
- When the user invokes `/capture-lesson` or `/finish-feature`, follow the corresponding Agent Skill under [`.ai/cursor/skills/`](../skills/) for classification, deduplication, Memory Bank updates, and wrap-up; do not edit `AGENTS.md` files as part of those workflows.
